% 02_key_and_accidentals.gmn -- audible test: a tune in Eb major,
% exercising \key<"e&"> (tonality-string form, lowercase = minor is
% NOT used here, this is major) plus explicit accidentals on every
% altered note -- GUIDO notes are always literal (see guido_import.clj's
% own KEY-IMPLIED ACCIDENTALS docstring note), so unlike ABC's example
% this one writes every flat/sharp/natural out by hand, including a
% double-sharp for variety.
[ \key<"e&"> \meter<"3/4">
  e&1/4 g&1/4 b&1/4 | c2/4 b&2/4 a2/4 | a##2/4 b&2/4 g&2/4 | e&2/2. ]
